.TH BOSWAS 1 "October 2026" "Boswas OS v1 Alpha" "Boswas OS"
.SH NAME
boswas, boswas-info, boswas-status \- Boswas OS status and administration tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B boswas
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.I command
.RI [ action ]
.br
.B boswas-info
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B boswas-status
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B boswas
reports the identity, configuration and security posture of a Boswas OS
device. All commands are read-only in v1 alpha and never print credentials,
tokens or key material.
.B boswas-info
is equivalent to
.BR "boswas info" ,
and
.B boswas-status
to
.BR "boswas status" .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B info
OS name and version, image build, Debian base, kernel, desktop, boot mode,
device identity and a compliance summary.
.TP
.B status
Run all local posture checks (Secure Boot, TPM, disk encryption, firewall,
AppArmor, audit, SSH server, root account, screen lock, USB policy, updates,
agent, enrollment).
.TP
.B security status
Security checks only.
.TP
.B device status
Device identity from /etc/boswas/device.conf and a non-sensitive hardware
summary.
.TP
.B policy status
Device policy state.
.TP
.B update status
Update channel and automatic security update state.
.TP
.B version
Version of the boswas tool.
.PP
.B app list
and
.B winapp list
are reserved for later phases and exit with status 69.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit a JSON document (schema "boswas-cli/1") instead of text. May be given
before or after the command.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success; for status commands, no check failed.
.TP
.B 1
At least one posture check failed.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.TP
.B 69
Command not available in this release.
.TP
.B 70
Internal error.
.SH NOTES
Compliance results are a local self-assessment against the Boswas OS v1
alpha baseline. They are not remote attestation.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/boswas/release
Boswas OS release identity.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/boswas/image-info
Metadata of the image this device was installed from.
.TP
.I /etc/boswas/device.conf
Device identity and enrollment state.
